  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They broke through the scoreless tie early and never looked back, turning a tied third into a blowout by the fifth.",
    "what_this_means": "J.T. Ginn gave them six clean innings and the bullpen didn't miss a beat. Medina struck out three across 1.2, Harris got four more in the ninth. The lineup did what it needed to do: Heim went 2-for-3 with a two-run shot, Langeliers added one of his own, and the team scratched out twelve hits against the Dodgers. They scored three in the fifth and that was the game. This is what a controlled win looks like for a team that has seen very few of them. No desperation, no grinding late, just clean baseball early and then a comfortable finish. Down 3.0 games with the division watching, they took one back.",
